{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a7f2c9e1-4b3d-4c6e-9f00-suppliers-bulk",
    "name": "Spendesk API — Suppliers bulk (create / patch / archive)",
    "description": "Flux aligné sur `scripts/test-supplier-bulk-operations.mjs` :\n1. Obtenir un access_token (client credentials)\n2. POST /v1/suppliers (corps = tableau)\n3. PATCH /v1/suppliers (corps = tableau { id, ... })\n4. PATCH /v1/experimental/suppliers/status\n\nImporter aussi l’environnement et renseigner `client_id` / `client_secret`. Scopes : au minimum `experimental:supplier:manage` pour les mutations.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Auth — Client credentials",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const code = pm.response.code;",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Token OK (200)', function () { pm.expect(code).to.eql(200); });",
              "if (j.access_token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('access_token', j.access_token);",
              "  console.log('access_token enregistré dans l’environnement');",
              "} else {",
              "  console.warn('Pas d\\'access_token dans la réponse');",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "basic",
          "basic": [
            { "key": "username", "value": "{{client_id}}", "type": "string" },
            { "key": "password", "value": "{{client_secret}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"grant_type\": \"client_credentials\"\n}"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/token",
        "description": "POST `/v1/auth/token` avec Basic Auth (client_id / client_secret). Le script Tests enregistre `access_token` dans l’environnement actif."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Suppliers — Bulk create (POST /v1/suppliers)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const t = Date.now() + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);",
              "pm.environment.set('bulk_run_tag', t);",
              "function vat() {",
              "  return 'FR' + String(Math.floor(1e10 + Math.random() * 9e10)).slice(0, 11);",
              "}",
              "pm.environment.set('bulk_vat_1', vat());",
              "pm.environment.set('bulk_vat_2', vat());",
              "pm.environment.set('bulk_vat_3', vat());"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Create 201', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201); });",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "const ids = [];",
              "if (j.item && j.item.id) {",
              "  ids.push(j.item.id);",
              "  pm.environment.set('supplier_id_' + ids.length, j.item.id);",
              "}",
              "if (Array.isArray(j.items)) {",
              "  j.items.forEach((it, i) => {",
              "    if (it.outcome === 'created' && it.supplier && it.supplier.id) {",
              "      ids.push(it.supplier.id);",
              "      pm.environment.set('supplier_id_' + ids.length, it.supplier.id);",
              "    }",
              "  });",
              "}",
              "pm.environment.set('supplier_ids_json', JSON.stringify(ids));",
              "console.log('IDs enregistrés: supplier_id_1..3 et supplier_ids_json', ids);"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest A {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n    \"primaryEmail\": \"bulk-a-{{bulk_run_tag}}@example.invalid\",\n    \"supplierDetails\": {\n      \"legalName\": \"BulkTest Legal A {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n      \"vatNumber\": \"{{bulk_vat_1}}\",\n      \"country\": \"FR\",\n      \"city\": \"Lyon\",\n      \"zipcode\": \"69001\",\n      \"address\": \"10 rue Test Bulk\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest B {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n    \"primaryEmail\": \"bulk-b-{{bulk_run_tag}}@example.invalid\",\n    \"supplierDetails\": {\n      \"legalName\": \"BulkTest Legal B {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n      \"vatNumber\": \"{{bulk_vat_2}}\",\n      \"country\": \"FR\",\n      \"city\": \"Lyon\",\n      \"zipcode\": \"69001\",\n      \"address\": \"10 rue Test Bulk\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest C {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n    \"primaryEmail\": \"bulk-c-{{bulk_run_tag}}@example.invalid\",\n    \"supplierDetails\": {\n      \"legalName\": \"BulkTest Legal C {{bulk_run_tag}}\",\n      \"vatNumber\": \"{{bulk_vat_3}}\",\n      \"country\": \"FR\",\n      \"city\": \"Lyon\",\n      \"zipcode\": \"69001\",\n      \"address\": \"10 rue Test Bulk\"\n    }\n  }\n]"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/v1/suppliers",
        "description": "Corps = **tableau** de `supplierToCreate`. Les IDs créés sont stockés en `supplier_id_1`, `supplier_id_2`, `supplier_id_3` et `supplier_ids_json`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "03 Suppliers — Bulk patch (PATCH /v1/suppliers)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Patch 200', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"{{supplier_id_1}}\",\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest UPDATED-1 {{bulk_run_tag}}\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"{{supplier_id_2}}\",\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest UPDATED-2 {{bulk_run_tag}}\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"{{supplier_id_3}}\",\n    \"name\": \"BulkTest UPDATED-3 {{bulk_run_tag}}\"\n  }\n]"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/v1/suppliers",
        "description": "Corps = **tableau** d’objets avec au minimum `id` + champs à modifier. Exécuter **02** avant pour remplir les variables."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "04 Suppliers — Bulk archive (PATCH experimental status)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Archive 200', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200); });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{access_token}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"supplierIds\": {{supplier_ids_json}},\n  \"isArchived\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": "{{base_url}}/v1/experimental/suppliers/status",
        "description": "Bulk archive via `supplierIds` + `isArchived`. `supplier_ids_json` est un tableau JSON produit par la requête **02**."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://beta-sandbox.api.trunk.spendesk.services"
    }
  ]
}
